# libpdx-cap release manifest — v1.0.1
#
# Format: manifest.pdxsig v0.1 (per design/tooling/plan.md §6.3 in
# paideia-os). The @-directives below are the source of record for a
# release; the dual-signature block at the bottom is populated by the
# signing bot (paideia-os T-INFRA-002) once the ML-DSA-65 sign
# primitive's userspace linkage lands (paideia-as v0.33-crypto,
# issues #1302–#1306). The hash tree is stable and re-verifiable now.
#
# Trust model per design/tooling/plan.md §6.2: dual ML-DSA-65
# signatures under (author_pk, paideia_root_pk). `pkg install` refuses
# any package where either signature fails to verify against a trusted
# key. The reserved slots below encode the exact 3309-byte body
# ML-DSA-65 will produce; the signing bot overwrites bytes in place
# without changing manifest byte count.
#
# NOTE — v1.0.0 WITHDRAWN; this is v1.0.1
# ----------------------------------------
# `v1.0.0` (tag `27c29e2`) attested a tree that does not assemble
# (`src/cap.pdx:214` was missing a `;` before a fall-through label;
# fixed three commits later at `da38a9e`, which the v1.0.0 tag
# predates) and, independently, a hash tree that had already gone
# stale for two artifacts by the time anyone re-verified it
# (`README.md`, `src/cap.pdx`). Libpdx-cap#19 (ENH-001) cuts this
# v1.0.1 manifest from a tree that has actually been assembled
# (`paideia-as check` clean on every `src/*.pdx` + `tests/*.pdx`) and
# whose M4 witnesses have actually been linked and run
# (`bash tools/run-tests.sh` exits 0) — the first time either of
# those has been true for a tagged libpdx-cap release. `v1.0.0` is
# withdrawn; do not resolve `libpdx-cap @ ^1.0` to that tag.
#
# NOTE — signature status (unchanged since 1.0.0)
# -------------------------------------------------
# The two @-sig-slot blocks below carry 3309-byte all-zero placeholder
# bodies. This is INTENTIONAL because:
#
#   (1) The paideia-as v0.33-crypto ML-DSA-65 SIGN primitive is not
#       yet exposed as a userspace intrinsic (paideia-as-team
#       deliverable; see .plans/m3-002-notes.md). VERIFY is exposed
#       (paideia-as v0.33 crypto-kdf tag reachable), so downstream
#       consumers can already call `ml_dsa_65_verify` — it will report
#       failure against the placeholder until the signing bot re-signs.
#
#   (2) The `pkgs.paideia-os` mirror (paideia-os T-INFRA-001) and the
#       signing bot host (paideia-os T-INFRA-002) do not yet exist.
#       When both come online the bot re-signs this manifest in place
#       and republishes to `pkgs.paideia-os/main/libpdx-cap/1.0.1/`;
#       the byte-count-preserving slot shape means downstream verifiers
#       ingest the same file at the same URL.
#
# The 1.0.1 tag on `github.com/paideia-os/libpdx-cap` is the immutable
# authoritative source; the mirror push is a distribution optimisation.

@manifest         libpdx-cap 1.0.1
@license          MIT
@wave             R49
@kind             library
@author           paideia-os-team
@created          2026-08-25
@format-version   0.1
@hash-algorithm   SHA-256
@sig-algorithm    ML-DSA-65
@sig-length       3309
@upstream         github.com/paideia-os/libpdx-cap
@upstream-tag     v1.0.1
@mirror-target    pkgs.paideia-os/main/libpdx-cap/1.0.1/
@doc-consumer     doc libpdx-cap  (via doc/libpdx-cap.pdxdoc)

@dependencies     (none)                             # libpdx-cap.M1..M5 has no library deps
@paideia-as-min   0.33                               # mov_b + @align on .bss
@paideia-os-min   R48                                # KIND_USER + KIND_TTY + PdxFS-substrate

@milestones-closed
    M1  #1 #2          scaffold + caps.decl parser
    M2  #3 #4 #5       manifest_verify + narrow + extra-cap reject
    M3  #6 #7          KIND_USER_ref + signed-inode helpers
    M4  #8 #9          round-trip fuzz + caps.decl matrix
    M5  #10            dual-signed release + .pdxdoc + mirror push
    ENH #11 #12 #13 #14 #15 #16 #17     v1.x fixes + release hygiene (v1.0.0 withdrawn)

@artifacts                                                                                sha256                                                              bytes
